.TH FSTRACE-DAEMON 1 "2026-11-06" "fstrace 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fstrace-daemon \- privileged eBPF daemon for fstrace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fstrace-daemon
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B fstrace-daemon
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.RB [ -V | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fstrace-daemon
is the privileged half of
.BR fstrace (1).
It loads eBPF, owns the kernel maps and ring buffer, and serves unprivileged
.BR fstrace (1)
clients over a Unix socket.
.PP
The kernel authenticates each client's actual fork using a one-use token.
The daemon rejects supplied PIDs and duplicate ownership, then routes events
by session and task lifetime. It never inspects
.IR /proc ,
and can run in a different PID and mount namespace from clients.
.PP
This is the only component that requires elevated privileges
.RB ( CAP_BPF
and
.BR CAP_PERFMON ,
or
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN );
the
.BR fstrace (1)
client runs as an ordinary user. The daemon runs in the foreground until
killed; use a service manager, or background it, to keep it running.
.PP
Use matching client and daemon builds; FSTRACE2 rejects the old PID-only
handshake. Kernels need BTF, BPF trampolines, ring buffers and ftrace support:
x64 5.8+, ARM64 6.4+ with ftrace direct calls.
Every compiled hook is required; load or attach failures stop startup
before the socket is published.
.PP
Custom client seccomp profiles must allow clone with CLONE_PIDFD,
pidfd_send_signal and waitid with P_PIDFD.
The cross-UID report-pipe helper also needs close_range (Linux 5.9+).
Tracing requires no-new-privileges on the child, not the client or embedding
caller. Traced sudo, setuid executables and file capabilities cannot elevate.
.PP
Limits are 64 connections and 1,024 queued events per client on each side.
Loss or overload fails the trace. Completion and socket writes have 30-second
deadlines.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Listen on the Unix socket
.IR PATH .
Overrides
.BR FSTRACE_SOCKET .
Defaults to
.BR /run/fstrace/fstrace.sock .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH SOCKET ACTIVATION
The daemon implements the systemd
.BR sd_listen_fds (3)
protocol. If launched via socket activation \(em with
.B LISTEN_FDS
and
.B LISTEN_PID
set \(em it adopts the listening socket systemd already bound and passed to it;
otherwise it binds the socket itself. Ready\-to\-use
.B fstrace.socket
and
.B fstrace.service
units, an init script, and a container image ship under
.IR packaging/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FSTRACE_SOCKET
Socket path to bind (default
.BR /run/fstrace/fstrace.sock ).
The
.B \-\-socket
option takes precedence. Must match the clients.
.TP
.B FSTRACE_PROFILE
Set to
.B 1
in both the daemon and client environments to emit aggregate daemon, client,
and eBPF performance summaries through the logging destination.
.TP
.BR FSTRACE_LOG_FILE ", " FSTRACE_LOG_DIR
Write log output to an explicit file, or to a per\-process file
.RI ( fstrace-daemon.log )
under a directory, respectively.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log verbosity using
.BR tracing / env\-filter
syntax, e.g.
.BR fstrace=trace .
.B FSTRACE_DEBUG=1
is shorthand for
.BR fstrace=debug .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Runs until stopped. Exits
.B 1
on a fatal startup error (for example, if the eBPF programs cannot be loaded),
printing a diagnostic to standard error. Exits
.B 2
on an invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the daemon (backgrounded) and then trace without
.BR sudo :
.PP
.RS
.B sudo fstrace-daemon &
.br
.B fstrace ls 3>&1
.RE
.PP
Run a private daemon on a custom socket:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo fstrace-daemon --socket /tmp/fst.sock &
.br
.B FSTRACE_SOCKET=/tmp/fst.sock fstrace ls 3>&1
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fstrace (1),
.BR sd_listen_fds (3)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/bmiddha/fstrace
fstrace on GitHub
.UE
